[statement]
The removals a removal pulls go in the order of apk's table of names, each
at the first of the names it carries and provides: `sh` provides
`/bin/sh` at no version, which `suh`, `tl` and `mccc` need, listed in that
order. apk removes them in the order their names' buckets come, `tl`,
`mccc`, then `suh`, and then `sh`.

[repository]
P:x
V:1

[installed]
P:sh
V:1
p:/bin/sh

P:suh
V:1
D:/bin/sh

P:tl
V:1
D:/bin/sh

P:mccc
V:1
D:/bin/sh

P:k
V:1

[request]
x

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove tl 1
remove mccc 1
remove suh 1
remove sh 1
remove k 1
install x 1
